{% extends "layouts/app.njk" %}
{% from "govuk/components/summary-list/macro.njk" import govukSummaryList %}
{% from "govuk/components/tag/macro.njk" import govukTag %}
{% from "govuk/components/inset-text/macro.njk" import govukInsetText %}

{#
  One email's content, on a page of its own rather than in the tab's table: a body is several paragraphs and would
  destroy a govukTable's scannability, and the tab is what a caseworker loads every time where the content is what
  they occasionally need. Decision 14 of docs/plans/notify-2-caseworker-email-tab.md.

  THE BODY IS PLAIN TEXT AND RENDERS THROUGH AUTOESCAPING. api's `EmailHistoryResponse.body` is the text
  rendering of the template, not the branded HTML the applicant read — the two are different fields of different
  shapes (decision 12). So: no `| safe`, and NOT the preview's sandboxed srcdoc iframe, which exists for the
  other one. Newlines are preserved by `app-email-body` (white-space: pre-wrap) rather than by markup, and
  Notify's Markdown-flavoured bullets are shown as the `*` they arrive as — passing caseworker free text through
  a Markdown renderer would put it back into an unescaped render for no gain. email-detail.njk.test.ts asserts
  that a body containing `<script>` appears as visible text.

  The heading says this is the wording rather than the email (decision 13), because the applicant saw Notify's
  branding around it and "that is not what they got" is the objection this page has to survive.

  Nothing here may read as proof of receipt. api knows GOV.UK Notify accepted the send and nothing more, so the
  state's words come from the domain's label map and the hint spells out what they mean — decision 10, and the
  test asserts no "Delivered", "Viewed", "Opened" or "Downloaded" survives on the page.
#}
{% block content %}
<div class="govuk-grid-row">
  <div class="govuk-grid-column-two-thirds">

    <span class="govuk-caption-l">{{ case.displayReference }}</span>
    <h1 class="govuk-heading-xl govuk-!-margin-bottom-4">{{ heading }}</h1>

    {#
      Every attachment the email carried. Empty for every email today — the one shipped template attaches
      nothing and notify-4 is blocked on document generation — so this renders "None" rather than an empty cell,
      which beside "Documents attached" would read as a question the page failed to answer.
    #}
    {% set documentsCell %}
      {% if email.documents.length %}
        <ul class="govuk-list govuk-!-margin-bottom-0">
          {% for document in email.documents %}<li>{{ document.name }}</li>{% endfor %}
        </ul>
      {% else %}
        {{ noDocuments }}
      {% endif %}
    {% endset %}

    {% set metadataRows = [
      { key: { text: templateLabel }, value: { text: email.template } },
      { key: { text: subjectLabel }, value: { text: email.subject } },
      { key: { text: recipientLabel }, value: { text: email.recipient } },
      { key: { text: stateLabel }, value: { html: govukTag({ text: email.state, classes: email.stateTagClasses }) } }
    ] %}

    {#
      api's own prose on a failure, and the row that makes a failed email actionable: "the recipient address was
      rejected" tells a caseworker to ring the applicant where "Failed" alone tells them only to worry. Absent
      rather than empty when api published none.
    #}
    {% if email.failureReason %}
      {% set metadataRows = (metadataRows.push({ key: { text: failureLabel }, value: { text: email.failureReason } }), metadataRows) %}
    {% endif %}

    {% set metadataRows = (metadataRows.push(
      { key: { text: createdLabel }, value: { text: email.sentBy + ", " + email.sentOn } },
      { key: { text: documentsLabel }, value: { html: documentsCell } }
    ), metadataRows) %}

    {{ govukSummaryList({ rows: metadataRows }) }}

    <p class="govuk-hint">{{ stateHint }}</p>

    <h2 class="govuk-heading-m">{{ bodyHeading }}</h2>

    {#
      The body, or the sentence saying why there is none — exactly one of the two, guaranteed by the view model.
      A blank panel here reads as a bug, and the three reasons an email has no wording are three different
      reassurances (decision 15), so the view model picks the sentence and this template only places it.
    #}
    {% if email.body %}
      <p class="govuk-body">{{ bodyCaption }}</p>
      <div class="govuk-body app-email-body">{{ email.body }}</div>
    {% else %}
      {{ govukInsetText({ text: email.missingBody }) }}
    {% endif %}

    <p class="govuk-body">
      <a class="govuk-link" href="{{ case.id | casePath }}#emails">{{ backToCase }}</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</div>
{% endblock %}
